{"name":"Pele","hex":"#da702c","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pele","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Hawaiian goddess of fire and volcanos.","A female given name from Hawaiian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pele"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pele (deity)","blocks":[{"text":"In Hawaiian religion, Pele is the goddess of volcanoes and fire and the creator of the Hawaiian Islands. Often referred to as \"Madame Pele\" or \"Tūtū Pele\" as a sign of respect, she is a well-known deity within Hawaiian mythology and is notable for her contemporary presence and cultural influence as an enduring figure from ancient Hawaii. Epithets of the goddess include Pele-honua-mea and Ka wahine ʻai honua."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/The_goddess_pele_by_arthur_johnsen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pele_(deity)","wikidata":"Q1133063"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/The_goddess_pele_by_arthur_johnsen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/The_goddess_pele_by_arthur_johnsen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_goddess_pele_by_arthur_johnsen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Halema%27uma%27u_Crater_at_Night.jpg/500px-Halema%27uma%27u_Crater_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Halema%27uma%27u_Crater_at_Night.jpg/1280px-Halema%27uma%27u_Crater_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Halema%27uma%27u_Crater_at_Night.jpg/5